---
title: Advanced
order: 6
description: Cherry-pick, reset, revert, reflog, clean, and worktree
tags: [git, cherry-pick, reset, revert, reflog, clean, worktree]
---

Operations that rewrite history or manage multiple working trees.

@code bash
# Cherry-pick: apply specific commits to current branch
git cherry-pick abc1234
git cherry-pick abc1234 def5678          # multiple commits
git cherry-pick main~3..main            # range of commits
git cherry-pick --no-commit abc1234     # apply without committing
git cherry-pick --abort                  # cancel on conflict
git cherry-pick --continue              # after resolving conflicts

@text
Reset moves the branch pointer. Affects staging area and working tree
depending on the mode. Only use on unpublished commits.

@code bash
# Reset modes
git reset --soft HEAD~1          # undo commit, keep changes staged
git reset --mixed HEAD~1         # undo commit, keep changes unstaged (default)
git reset --hard HEAD~1          # undo commit, discard all changes (dangerous)
git reset HEAD file.go           # unstage a file (keep changes)

# Reset to a specific commit
git reset --soft abc1234
git reset --hard origin/main     # match remote exactly (dangerous)

@text
Revert creates a new commit that undoes a previous commit. Safe for
published history since it does not rewrite commits.

@code bash
# Revert a commit
git revert abc1234
git revert HEAD                  # revert last commit
git revert --no-commit abc1234   # apply revert without committing
git revert --no-commit HEAD~3..HEAD  # revert last 3 commits
git revert -m 1 abc1234         # revert a merge commit (keep parent 1)
git revert --abort               # cancel on conflict

@text
Reflog records every change to branch tips and HEAD. Your safety net
for recovering lost commits.

@code bash
# View reflog
git reflog                       # HEAD movements
git reflog show main             # specific branch
git reflog --date=relative       # with timestamps

# Recover a lost commit
git reflog                       # find the commit hash
git checkout abc1234             # inspect it
git branch recovered abc1234    # create branch to save it

# Recover after bad reset
git reflog
git reset --hard HEAD@{3}       # go back to state 3 moves ago

# Reflog entries expire (default 90 days for reachable, 30 unreachable)
git reflog expire --expire=now --all   # force expire (rarely needed)

@text
Clean removes untracked files from the working tree. Useful for build
artifacts not in .gitignore.

@code bash
# Preview what would be removed
git clean -n                     # dry run
git clean -nd                    # dry run including directories

# Remove untracked files
git clean -f                     # force required (safety)
git clean -fd                    # include untracked directories
git clean -fx                    # include ignored files
git clean -fxd                   # untracked + ignored + directories
git clean -i                     # interactive mode

@text
Worktree lets you check out multiple branches simultaneously in separate
directories. Each worktree has its own working tree and index.

@code bash
# Create a worktree
git worktree add ../hotfix main           # new worktree from main
git worktree add ../experiment            # new branch + worktree
git worktree add -b fix-99 ../fix origin/main  # new branch from remote

# List worktrees
git worktree list

# Remove a worktree
git worktree remove ../hotfix
git worktree remove --force ../broken    # if unclean

# Prune stale worktree metadata
git worktree prune

# Move a worktree
git worktree move ../hotfix ../urgent-fix
